{
    "_doc": "Living animals of the inner map (world/innerMap/animals.js places and moves them; ui/innerMapAnimals.js draws them, hooks them into hunting, fights and butchering). Sheets: walk / attack / death, each a 4x4 grid of 128px cells, a row per direction (up, left, down, right), four frames a row; every sheet of one animal shares the cell and the feet anchor, so they line up. Built from the hand-out sheets by scripts/build-animal-sheets.py, which also gives each drawTiles (the cell's width in tiles). Speeds are tiles a second; distances are tiles; hp and bite as the player's health. temper: skittish (flee), defensive (flee; may turn and fight when hurt or cornered: fightChance), territorial (warn inside threatRadius, charge inside chargeRadius or if you stay), hunter (notice: stalk — rolls aggression, more by night; packs decide together). fleeBelow: the health share it breaks off at; maxBites: a bout's bites before it backs off (0 = no limit). livestock: a settlement's flocks — killing one is theft (value: its worth).",
